duct brochure is considerably _____ than the previous version.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Than signals a comparative form; the multi-syllable adjective detailed uses more.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(51,3,9,'PART_1','EASY','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q01','Which statement best describes the scene?','[Scene description] In an office, a woman is placing labeled folders onto a tall shelf.',NULL,NULL,'The woman is actively arranging files on a shelf; the other statements introduce actions or objects not present.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(52,3,9,'PART_2','EASY','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q02','Choose the best response.','[Audio script] When will the replacement package arrive?',NULL,NULL,'A when-question requires a time response. By noon tomorrow directly answers it.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(53,3,9,'PART_2','EASY','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q03','Choose the best response.','[Audio script] Why don\'t we move the budget meeting to Friday?',NULL,NULL,'Why don\'t we introduces a suggestion. That\'s a good idea is the natural response.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(54,3,9,'PART_2','MEDIUM','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q04','Choose the best response.','[Audio script] Who is leading the orientation session this afternoon?',NULL,NULL,'A who-question asks for a person; Ms. Delgado from Human Resources is the only appropriate response.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(55,3,9,'PART_3','MEDIUM','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q05','What will the man most likely do next?','[Audio script]\nWoman: The client meeting has been moved from Room 310 to Room 402.\nMan: I already left the printed agendas in Room 310.\nWoman: I\'ll notify the participants while you bring the agendas upstairs.',NULL,NULL,'The woman explicitly asks the man to bring the agendas upstairs to the new room.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(56,3,9,'PART_3','MEDIUM','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q06','Where should the man wait for the shuttle?','[Audio script]\nMan: My train arrives at Central Station at 8:40. Is the hotel shuttle still available then?\nWoman: Yes, it leaves the station every thirty minutes until ten. Wait near Exit B.',NULL,NULL,'The woman tells him to wait near Exit B.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(57,3,9,'PART_4','MEDIUM','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q07','Why has the flight been delayed?','[Audio script] Attention passengers: Flight 316 to Bangkok has been delayed by forty minutes because of heavy rain. Boarding will begin at Gate 12 at 6:20 p.m.',NULL,NULL,'The announcement states that heavy rain caused the delay.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(58,3,9,'PART_4','MEDIUM','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q08','What time will the branch close today?','[Audio script] This is a reminder that the Westside branch will close at 4:30 today for staff training. Normal business hours will resume tomorrow morning at nine.',NULL,NULL,'The announcement gives 4:30 as today\'s early closing time.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(59,3,9,'PART_4','MEDIUM','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q09','What should callers do to ask about a bill?','[Audio script] Thank you for calling Benson Medical Center. To schedule or change an appointment, press one. For billing questions, press two. To speak with a nurse, press three.',NULL,NULL,'The recording instructs callers with billing questions to press two.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(60,3,9,'PART_3','HARD','DEMO600:LIS-01:Q10','What problem are the speakers discussing?','[Audio script]\nWoman: The printer on the third floor is out of toner again.\nMan: I ordered two cartridges yesterday, but delivery isn\'t until Thursday.\nWoman: I\'ll use the second-floor printer for today\'s reports.',NULL,NULL,'They discuss a printer that cannot be used because it has no toner.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-09-25 00:09:24','2026-09-25 00:09:24'),(61,3,10,'PART_1','EASY','DEMO600:LIS-02: