ăn phòng','In the sentence \"The stationery cabinet is restocked every two weeks.\", the word \"stationery\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"stationery\" /ˈsteɪʃənri/ (danh từ) nghĩa là \"văn phòng phẩm\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"technician\", \"compliance\", \"photocopier\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1271,3,1052,'PART_5','MEDIUM','Nhân sự & tuyển dụng','The store hires _______ staff during the holiday season.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"temporary\" (tính từ) – tạm thời. Câu cần một tính từ mang nghĩa \"tạm thời\". Các phương án khác: \"spacious\" (rộng rãi), \"satisfied\" (hài lòng), \"affordable\" (giá phải chăng) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1272,3,1052,'PART_5','HARD','Nhân sự & tuyển dụng','Salaries are reviewed _______ in December.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"annually\" (trạng từ) – hằng năm. Câu cần một trạng từ mang nghĩa \"hằng năm\". Các phương án khác: \"recently\" (gần đây), \"steadily\" (đều đặn), \"separately\" (riêng rẽ) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1273,3,1052,'PART_5','EASY','Nhân sự & tuyển dụng','The strongest _______ has ten years of sales experience.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"candidate\" (danh từ) – ứng viên (được xem xét). Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"ứng viên (được xem xét)\". Các phương án khác: \"promotion\" (sự thăng chức), \"résumé\" (sơ yếu lý lịch), \"benefits\" (phúc lợi) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1274,3,1052,'PART_5','MEDIUM','Nhân sự & tuyển dụng','New hires attend a two-day _______ in their first week.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"orientation\" (danh từ) – buổi định hướng nhân viên mới. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"buổi định hướng nhân viên mới\". Các phương án khác: \"résumé\" (sơ yếu lý lịch), \"benefits\" (phúc lợi), \"applicant\" (ứng viên) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1275,3,1052,'PART_5','HARD','Nhân sự & tuyển dụng','The position offers competitive pay and generous _______.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"benefits\" (danh từ) – phúc lợi. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"phúc lợi\". Các phương án khác: \"orientation\" (buổi định hướng nhân viên mới), \"applicant\" (ứng viên), \"candidate\" (ứng viên (được xem xét)) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1276,3,1052,'PART_5','EASY','Nhân sự & tuyển dụng','The director will _______ at the end of the month.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"resign\" (động từ) – từ chức. Câu cần một động từ mang nghĩa \"từ chức\". Các phương án khác: \"recruit\" (tuyển dụng), \"evaluate\" (đánh giá), \"hire\" (thuê, tuyển) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1277,3,1053,'PART_5','HARD','Công nghệ & thiết bị','Our _______ computers will be replaced this year.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"outdated\" (tính từ) – lỗi thời. Câu cần một tính từ mang nghĩa \"lỗi thời\". Các phương án khác: \"experienced\" (có kinh nghiệm), \"annual\" (hằng năm), \"spacious\" (rộng rãi) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1278,3,1053,'PART_5','EASY','Công nghệ & thiết bị','Many staff members now work _______ twice a week.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"remotely\" (trạng từ) – từ xa. Câu cần một trạng từ mang nghĩa \"từ xa\". Các phương án khác: \"substantially\" (đáng kể), \"widely\" (rộng rãi), \"conveniently\" (một cách thuận tiện) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1279,3,1053,'PART_5','MEDIUM','Công nghệ & thiết bị','Change your _______ every three months.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"password\" (danh từ) – mật khẩu. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"mật khẩu\". Các phương án khác: \"upgrade\" (sự nâng cấp), \"software\" (phần mềm), \"malfunction\" (sự trục trặc) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1280,3,1053,'PART_5','HARD','Công nghệ & thiết bị','A _______ in the server caused the outage.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"malfunction\" (danh từ) – sự trục trặc. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"sự trục trặc\". Các phương án khác: \"device\" (thiết bị), \"upgrade\" (sự nâng cấp), \"software\" (phần mềm) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1281,3,1053,'PART_5','EASY','Công nghệ & thiết bị','The network _______ will improve connection speeds.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"upgrade\" (danh từ) – sự nâng cấp. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"sự nâng cấp\". Các phương án khác: \"password\" (mật khẩu), \"technician\" (kỹ thuật viên), \"device\" (thiết bị) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1282,3,1053,'GENERAL','MEDIUM','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"The new app is simple and user-friendly.\", the word \"user-friendly\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"user-friendly\" /ˌjuːzə ˈfrendli/ (tính từ) nghĩa là \"dễ sử dụng\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"innovative\", \"routine\", \"express\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1283,3,1054,'PART_5','HARD','Đảo ngữ trong văn bản trang trọng','Rarely ___ such strong sales in the first month of a product launch.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"Rarely\" đứng đầu → đảo trợ động từ: have we seen.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1284,3,1054,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Đảo ngữ trong văn bản trang trọng','Not only ___ the new system faster, but it is also cheaper to maintain.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not only + đảo ngữ với \"be\": is the new system.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1285,3,1054,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Đảo ngữ trong văn bản trang trọng','___ the report been submitted on time, the client would have approved the budget.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đảo ngữ loại 3: Had + S + V3.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1286,3,1054,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Đảo ngữ trong văn bản trang trọng','Only after the contract was signed ___ the construction begin.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"Only after + mệnh đề\" → đảo ngữ ở mệnh đề chính: did + S + V.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1287,3,1054,'PART_5','HARD','Đảo ngữ trong văn bản trang trọng','No sooner had the meeting started ___ the fire alarm went off.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cấu trúc cố định \"No sooner ... than\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1288,3,1054,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Tài chính & kế toán','Office rent is our largest monthly _______.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"expense\" (danh từ) – khoản chi. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"khoản chi\". Các phương án khác: \"invoice\" (hóa đơn thanh toán), \"audit\" (cuộc kiểm toán), \"estimate\" (bản ước tính) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1289,3,1055,'PART_5','HARD','Mệnh đề rút gọn và phân từ','Employees ___ in the training program must complete an online survey.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nhân viên tự tham gia (chủ động) → rút gọn V-ing.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1290,3,1055,'PART_5','HARD','Mệnh đề rút gọn và phân từ','The documents ___ by the legal department are ready for signature.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tài liệu được xem xét (bị động) → V3.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1291,3,1055,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Mệnh đề rút gọn và phân từ','___ the necessary approvals, the team began construction.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hành động nhận phê duyệt xảy ra trước → \"Having + V3\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1292,3,1055,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Mệnh đề rút gọn và phân từ','Once ___, the new policy will apply to all branches.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Rút gọn bị động \"Once (it is) approved\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1293,3,1055,'PART_5','HARD','Mệnh đề rút gọn và phân từ','Customers ___ to return an item must present the original receipt.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Khách hàng tự mong muốn (chủ động) → \"wishing\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1294,3,1055,'PART_5','HARD','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','This voucher is _______ until the end of the year.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"valid\" (tính từ) – có hiệu lực. Câu cần một tính từ mang nghĩa \"có hiệu lực\". Các phương án khác: \"round-trip\" (khứ hồi), \"qualified\" (đủ tiêu chuẩn), \"temporary\" (tạm thời) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1295,3,1056,'PART_7','EASY','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','Who is the letter intended for?','Dear Tenants,\n\nThis is a reminder that the current lease agreements for all units in Sunrise Office Building expire on June 30. Tenants who wish to renew must sign the new agreement by May 31. Please note that the monthly rent will increase by 5 percent, reflecting higher maintenance and utilities costs. In return, the building will install a new security system and upgrade the elevators this summer. Tenants who do not plan to renew are asked to inform the management office in writing at least 30 days before moving out.\n\nSunrise Property Management',NULL,NULL,'\"Dear Tenants\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1296,3,1056,'PART_7','EASY','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','What is the deadline for renewing a lease?','Dear Tenants,\n\nThis is a reminder that the current lease agreements for all units in Sunrise Office Building expire on June 30. Tenants who wish to renew must sign the new agreement by May 31. Please note that the monthly rent will increase by 5 percent, reflecting higher maintenance and utilities costs. In return, the building will install a new security system and upgrade the elevators this summer. Tenants who do not plan to renew are asked to inform the management office in writing at least 30 days before moving out.\n\nSunrise Property Management',NULL,NULL,'\"must sign the new agreement by May 31\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1297,3,1056,'PART_7','MEDIUM','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','Why will the rent increase?','Dear Tenants,\n\nThis is a reminder that the current lease agreements for all units in Sunrise Office Building expire on June 30. Tenants who wish to renew must sign the new agreement by May 31. Please note that the monthly rent will increase by 5 percent, reflecting higher maintenance and utilities costs. In return, the building will install a new security system and upgrade the elevators this summer. Tenants who do not plan to renew are asked to inform the management office in writing at least 30 days before moving out.\n\nSunrise Property Management',NULL,NULL,'\"reflecting higher maintenance and utilities costs\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1298,3,1056,'PART_7','HARD','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','What must tenants who are leaving do?','Dear Tenants,\n\nThis is a reminder that the current lease agreements for all units in Sunrise Office Building expire on June 30. Tenants who wish to renew must sign the new agreement by May 31. Please note that the monthly rent will increase by 5 percent, reflecting higher maintenance and utilities costs. In return, the building will install a new security system and upgrade the elevators this summer. Tenants who do not plan to renew are asked to inform the management office in writing at least 30 days before moving out.\n\nSunrise Property Management',NULL,NULL,'\"inform the management office in writing at least 30 days before\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1299,3,1056,'PART_7','EASY','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','Why did the client call?','Hoa Le (9:12 A.M.): Hi Minh, the client from Osaka just called. Their flight lands at 2 P.M., not 4.\nMinh Vu (9:14 A.M.): Oh no. The meeting room is booked until 3.\nHoa Le (9:15 A.M.): Could we use the small lounge on the 6th floor instead?\nMinh Vu (9:17 A.M.): That should work. I\'ll ask reception to prepare it and order some refreshments.\nHoa Le (9:18 A.M.): Perfect. I\'ll meet them at the airport.',NULL,NULL,'Chuyến bay hạ cánh lúc 2 giờ thay vì 4 giờ.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1300,3,1056,'PART_7','MEDIUM','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','At 9:17 A.M., what does Mr. Vu mean when he writes, \"That should work\"?','Hoa Le (9:12 A.M.): Hi Minh, the client from Osaka just called. Their flight lands at 2 P.M., not 4.\nMinh Vu (9:14 A.M.): Oh no. The meeting room is booked until 3.\nHoa Le (9:15 A.M.): Could we use the small lounge on the 6th floor instead?\nMinh Vu (9:17 A.M.): That should work. I\'ll ask reception to prepare it and order some refreshments.\nHoa Le (9:18 A.M.): Perfect. I\'ll meet them at the airport.',NULL,NULL,'Đồng ý dùng phòng nghỉ tầng 6 thay phòng họp.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1301,3,1056,'PART_7','EASY','Bất động sản & cơ sở vật chất','What will Ms. Le do next?','Hoa Le (9:12 A.M.): Hi Minh, the client from Osaka just called. Their flight lands at 2 P.M., not 4.\nMinh Vu (9:14 A.M.): Oh no. The meeting room is booked until 3.\nHoa Le (9:15 A.M.): Could we use the small lounge on the 6th floor instead?\nMinh Vu (9:17 A.M.): That should work. I\'ll ask reception to prepare it and order some refreshments.\nHoa Le (9:18 A.M.): Perfect. I\'ll meet them at the airport.',NULL,NULL,'\"I\'ll meet them at the airport.\"',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1302,3,1057,'PART_6','EASY','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','Choose the word for blank (1).','Dear Ms. Vy,\n\nThank you for staying at the Lotus Garden Hotel last weekend. We are sorry to hear that the air conditioner in your room was not working ___(1)___. As an apology, we would like to offer you a ___(2)___ night on your next visit. Simply mention code LG2025 when you make your reservation. ___(3)___ your feedback, we have also replaced the units in all rooms on the fifth floor.\n\nSincerely,\nHuy Tran, Guest Relations Manager',NULL,NULL,'Bổ nghĩa cho động từ \"working\" → trạng từ.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1303,3,1057,'PART_6','HARD','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','Choose the word for blank (2).','Dear Ms. Vy,\n\nThank you for staying at the Lotus Garden Hotel last weekend. We are sorry to hear that the air conditioner in your room was not working ___(1)___. As an apology, we would like to offer you a ___(2)___ night on your next visit. Simply mention code LG2025 when you make your reservation. ___(3)___ your feedback, we have also replaced the units in all rooms on the fifth floor.\n\nSincerely,\nHuy Tran, Guest Relations Manager',NULL,NULL,'\"complimentary night\" = đêm miễn phí.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1304,3,1057,'PART_6','MEDIUM','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','Choose the phrase for blank (3).','Dear Ms. Vy,\n\nThank you for staying at the Lotus Garden Hotel last weekend. We are sorry to hear that the air conditioner in your room was not working ___(1)___. As an apology, we would like to offer you a ___(2)___ night on your next visit. Simply mention code LG2025 when you make your reservation. ___(3)___ your feedback, we have also replaced the units in all rooms on the fifth floor.\n\nSincerely,\nHuy Tran, Guest Relations Manager',NULL,NULL,'Nhờ phản hồi của khách mà khách sạn thay máy → Thanks to.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1305,3,1057,'PART_5','HARD','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','Prices have risen, and we have adjusted our budget _______.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"accordingly\" (trạng từ) – theo đó, cho phù hợp. Câu cần một trạng từ mang nghĩa \"theo đó, cho phù hợp\". Các phương án khác: \"steadily\" (đều đặn), \"separately\" (riêng rẽ), \"promptly\" (ngay lập tức, đúng giờ) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1306,3,1057,'GENERAL','ADVANCED','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','In the sentence \"Attendance at the safety training is mandatory.\", the word \"mandatory\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"mandatory\" /ˈmændətəri/ (tính từ) nghĩa là \"bắt buộc\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"residential\", \"user-friendly\", \"available\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1307,3,1057,'GENERAL','HARD','Hợp đồng & pháp lý','In the sentence \"This voucher is valid until the end of the year.\", the word \"valid\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"valid\" /ˈvælɪd/ (tính từ) nghĩa là \"có hiệu lực\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"mandatory\", \"complimentary\", \"upcoming\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1308,3,1058,'GENERAL','HARD','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"Change your password every three months.\", the word \"password\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"password\" /ˈpɑːswɜːd/ (danh từ) nghĩa là \"mật khẩu\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"landlord\", \"shipment\", \"software\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1309,3,1058,'GENERAL','ADVANCED','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"A malfunction in the server caused the outage.\", the word \"malfunction\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"malfunction\" /ˌmælˈfʌŋkʃn/ (danh từ) nghĩa là \"sự trục trặc\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"supervisor\", \"itinerary\", \"fare\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1310,3,1058,'GENERAL','HARD','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"The network upgrade will improve connection speeds.\", the word \"upgrade\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"upgrade\" /ˈʌpɡreɪd/ (danh từ) nghĩa là \"sự nâng cấp\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"assembly line\", \"defect\", \"property\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1311,3,1058,'GENERAL','ADVANCED','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"A technician is fixing the projector in Room B.\", the word \"technician\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"technician\" /tekˈnɪʃn/ (danh từ) nghĩa là \"kỹ thuật viên\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"upgrade\", \"compliance\", \"stationery\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1312,3,1058,'GENERAL','HARD','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"Employees can download the form from the intranet.\", the word \"download\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"download\" /ˌdaʊnˈləʊd/ (động từ) nghĩa là \"tải xuống\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"recruit\", \"attend\", \"resolve\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1313,3,1058,'GENERAL','ADVANCED','Công nghệ & thiết bị','In the sentence \"You need a badge to access the server room.\", the word \"access\" is closest in meaning to:',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"access\" /ˈækses/ (động từ) nghĩa là \"truy cập\". Các phương án còn lại là nghĩa của \"download\", \"renew\", \"depart\".',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1314,3,1059,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Tài chính & kế toán','An external _______ will take place next month.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"audit\" (danh từ) – cuộc kiểm toán. Câu cần một danh từ mang nghĩa \"cuộc kiểm toán\". Các phương án khác: \"estimate\" (bản ước tính), \"invoice\" (hóa đơn thanh toán), \"expense\" (khoản chi) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1315,3,1059,'PART_5','HARD','Tài chính & kế toán','The board must _______ any expense over $10,000.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"approve\" (động từ) – phê duyệt. Câu cần một động từ mang nghĩa \"phê duyệt\". Các phương án khác: \"exceed\" (vượt quá), \"deposit\" (gửi (tiền)), \"allocate\" (phân bổ) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00'),(1316,3,1059,'PART_5','ADVANCED','Tài chính & kế toán','You can _______ checks at any of our branches.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Đáp án: \"deposit\" (động từ) – gửi (tiền). Câu cần một động từ mang nghĩa \"gửi (tiền)\". Các phương án khác: \"exceed\" (vượt quá), \"approve\" (phê duyệt), \"allocate\" (phân bổ) không hợp nghĩa.',1.00,'ACTIVE','2026-10-05 09:00:00','2026-10-05 09:00:00');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `questions` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

--
-- Table structure for table `reading_activities`
--

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `reading_activities`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `reading_activities` (
  `id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `course_week_id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL,
  `lesson_id` bigint unsigned DEFAULT NULL,
  `created_by_teacher_id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL,
  `title` varchar(200) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL,
  `description` text CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci,
  `instruction` text CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci,
  `passage` longtext CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci,
  `passage_format` enum('PLAIN','MARKDOWN') CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL DEFAULT 'MARKDOWN',
  `toeic_part` enum('PART_6','PART_7','GENERAL') CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PART_7',
  `passage_type` enum('SINGLE','DOUBLE','TRIPLE') CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL DEFAULT 'SINGLE',
  `status` enum('DRAFT','PUBLISHED','HIDDEN') CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL DEFAULT 'DRAFT',
  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  KEY `idx_reading_week_status` (`course_week_id`,`status`),
  KEY `idx_reading_lesson` (`lesson_id`),
  KEY `fk_reading_teacher` (`created_by_teacher_id`),
  CONSTRAINT `fk_reading_lesson` FOREIGN KEY (`lesson_id`) REFERENCES `lessons` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL,
  CONSTRAINT `fk_reading_teacher` FOREIGN KEY (`created_by_teacher_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT,
  CONSTRAINT `fk_reading_week` FOREIGN KEY (`course_week_id`) REFERENCES `course_weeks` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=3031 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

--
-- Dumping data for table `reading_activities`
--

LOCK TABLES `reading_activities` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `reading_activities` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `reading_activities` VALUES (3001,1,5,3,'Part 7: Memo — Lobby Renovation Update',NULL,'Đọc bản ghi nhớ gửi nhân viên văn phòng và trả lời 3 câu hỏi.','**MEMO**\nTo: All Harlow Street office staff\nFrom: Dana Whitfield, Facilities Manager\nDate: March 4\nSubject: Lobby renovation progress\n\nWork on the main lobby is moving faster than expected. The contractors are currently installing the new reception desk, and the electricians are replacing the ceiling lights this week. Because of this, the front entrance will remain closed until Friday, March 8. Please use the side entrance on Carver Lane in the meantime.\n\nWe are also updating the visitor sign-in process. Starting next Monday, guests will register on a tablet at the reception desk instead of signing a paper log. Reception staff are attending a short training session on the new system this Thursday afternoon.\n\nFinally, the building\'s two elevators are being inspected on Wednesday morning. One elevator will be out of service from 9:00 to 11:00 A.M. If you are expecting deliveries during that time, please ask the courier to use the freight elevator at the back of the building.\n\nThank you for your patience while we complete these improvements.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 01:00:00','2026-09-01 01:00:00'),(3002,3,10,3,'Part 7: Text Messages — Brochures for the Client',NULL,'Đọc chuỗi tin nhắn và trả lời 2 câu hỏi. Chú ý câu hỏi về ý của người viết.','**Marcus Bell (10:12 A.M.)**\nHi Leah, are you still at the printing shop? The client just moved our presentation to 2:00 this afternoon.\n\n**Leah Ortiz (10:14 A.M.)**\nI\'m here now. They said the brochures won\'t be ready until 1:30.\n\n**Marcus Bell (10:15 A.M.)**\nThat\'s cutting it close. Could they print just twenty copies first?\n\n**Leah Ortiz (10:17 A.M.)**\nI asked, and they can have twenty ready by noon. The rest can be delivered to the office tomorrow morning.\n\n**Marcus Bell (10:18 A.M.)**\nPerfect. Twenty is plenty for today\'s meeting. Please also pick up the poster board we ordered last week.\n\n**Leah Ortiz (10:20 A.M.)**\nWill do. I\'ll head back as soon as everything is packed, and I\'ll put the brochures in the small conference room.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 02:00:00','2026-09-01 02:00:00'),(3003,5,13,3,'Part 7: Schedule — Library Career Workshops',NULL,'Đọc thông báo kèm lịch hội thảo (chú ý ngày, giờ, phòng) và trả lời 3 câu hỏi.','## Greenfield Public Library — Spring Career Workshops\n\nAll workshops are free, but space is limited. Register at the front desk or call 555-0142 at least two days before the session you wish to attend.\n\n| Date | Workshop | Room | Time |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| April 3 | Writing an Effective Résumé | Room 2B | 6:00–7:30 P.M. |\n| April 10 | Preparing for Job Interviews | Room 2B | 6:00–7:30 P.M. |\n| April 17 | Building a Professional Online Profile | Computer Lab | 5:30–7:00 P.M. |\n| April 24 | Starting a Small Business | Main Hall | 6:30–8:30 P.M. |\n\nParticipants in the April 17 session should bring a valid library card to log in to the lab computers. The April 24 workshop will be led by Hannah Cole, owner of Cole\'s Bakery, who opened her first shop with a loan from a local community fund. Light refreshments will be served at every session.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 03:00:00','2026-09-01 03:00:00'),(3004,6,14,3,'Part 6: Notice — Parking Garage Maintenance',NULL,'Chọn đáp án phù hợp nhất cho mỗi chỗ trống (131)–(134) trong thông báo.','**NOTICE TO ALL TENANTS**\n\nThe parking garage at Westbrook Tower will undergo scheduled maintenance from Monday, June 9, to Wednesday, June 11. During this period, crews will repaint the parking lines and (131) ------- the drainage system on every level.\n\nLevels 1 and 2 will be closed on Monday and Tuesday. Vehicles left on closed levels after 7:00 A.M. may be moved at the owner\'s expense. Level 3 will remain (132) ------- throughout the maintenance period, so tenants are encouraged to park there. (133) -------. Overflow parking will also be available at the Fulton Street lot, located one block north of the building.\n\nWe understand that this work may cause some inconvenience. (134) ------- questions about the schedule, please contact the building management office at extension 210.','MARKDOWN','PART_6','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 04:00:00','2026-09-01 04:00:00'),(3005,6,15,3,'Part 6: E-mail — Welcome to the Design Team',NULL,'Chọn đáp án phù hợp nhất cho mỗi chỗ trống (131)–(134) trong e-mail.','To: Priya Raman <praman@kestrelmedia.com>\nFrom: Tom Ashford <tashford@kestrelmedia.com>\nDate: August 18\nSubject: Your first week\n\nDear Ms. Raman,\n\nOn behalf of everyone at Kestrel Media, welcome to the design team! We are (131) ------- to have someone with your experience joining us.\n\nYour first day will begin at 9:00 A.M. with a short orientation in Conference Room A. Afterward, a member of the IT department will help you set up your laptop and e-mail account. (132) -------. Please bring a photo ID so that security can issue your building pass.\n\nDuring your first week, you will (133) ------- with Jenna Lee, our senior designer, on the autumn catalog. This project will give you a clear picture of how our team works with clients.\n\nIf anything is unclear, feel free to contact me (134) ------- at extension 305.\n\nBest regards,\nTom Ashford\nDesign Manager','MARKDOWN','PART_6','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 05:00:00','2026-09-01 05:00:00'),(3006,7,16,3,'Part 7: Two E-mails — Booking a Meeting Room',NULL,'Đọc hai e-mail (chuyển tab Văn bản 1 / 2) và trả lời 5 câu hỏi. Có câu cần đối chiếu cả hai văn bản.','## E-mail 1\nTo: Facilities Desk\nFrom: Rachel Kim, Marketing\nDate: Tuesday, May 6\nSubject: Room request for May 15\n\nHello,\n\nI would like to reserve a meeting room for a client workshop on Thursday, May 15, from 1:00 to 4:00 P.M. We expect fourteen participants, so we need a room that seats at least fifteen people. The session will include a video presentation, so a projector and a screen are essential.\n\nIf possible, we would also like coffee and pastries to be set up by 12:45 P.M. Please charge the catering to the marketing department\'s budget code, MK-208.\n\nThank you,\nRachel Kim\n\n## E-mail 2\nTo: Rachel Kim\nFrom: Victor Lam, Facilities Desk\nDate: Wednesday, May 7\nSubject: RE: Room request for May 15\n\nDear Ms. Kim,\n\nThank you for your request. Unfortunately, the Harbor Room, which seats twenty, is already booked that afternoon. I have reserved the Garden Room for you instead. It holds sixteen people and has a built-in projector, but the screen is currently being repaired, so I will bring a portable one from storage.\n\nThe catering company needs orders at least five business days in advance, so I have placed yours today. Please note that they can deliver no earlier than 1:00 P.M. on the 15th.\n\nBest,\nVictor Lam','MARKDOWN','PART_7','DOUBLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 06:00:00','2026-09-01 06:00:00'),(3007,7,17,3,'Part 7: Notice and Flyer — Riverside Food Festival',NULL,'Đọc thông báo tuyển gian hàng và tờ rơi đính kèm (ảnh), rồi trả lời 4 câu hỏi.','## Call for Food Vendors\n\nThe Riverside Food Festival is returning to Harbor Park this summer, and the organizing committee is now accepting applications from local food vendors. Last year\'s festival attracted more than 12,000 visitors over two days, and we expect an even larger crowd this year.\n\nEach vendor will be given a 3-by-3-meter tent space, two folding tables, and access to electricity. Vendors must provide their own cooking equipment and are responsible for keeping their area clean throughout the event.\n\nApplications must be submitted online by May 31. The application fee is $150, which will be refunded in full to applicants who are not selected. Successful applicants will be notified by e-mail no later than June 14.\n\nPlease see the attached festival flyer for dates, opening hours, and parking information. Questions may be sent to vendors@riversidefest.org.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 07:00:00','2026-09-01 07:00:00'),(3008,8,18,3,'Part 7: Article — Small Breaks, Big Results',NULL,'Đọc bài báo và trả lời 4 câu hỏi, trong đó có một câu chèn câu vào vị trí [1]–[4].','## Small Breaks, Big Results\n\nA growing number of companies are encouraging employees to step away from their desks during the workday. [1] Research from several universities suggests that short, regular breaks help people stay focused for longer periods.\n\nAt Dalton Analytics, a data firm with 300 employees, managers introduced a \"ten-minute rule\" last year. Staff are asked to take a ten-minute break after every ninety minutes of work. [2] According to human resources director Lena Park, the number of errors in client reports dropped by almost 20 percent within six months.\n\nNot everyone was convinced at first. Some team leaders worried that the breaks would slow down urgent projects. [3] To address these concerns, the company allowed teams to schedule breaks around important deadlines rather than at fixed times.\n\nMs. Park says the key is consistency. \"A break only works if people actually take it,\" she explains. [4] The company now sends a gentle reminder through its messaging app when employees have been working without a pause for more than two hours.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 08:00:00','2026-09-01 08:00:00'),(3009,8,18,3,'Part 7: Company Newsletter (PDF) — The Northbridge Bulletin',NULL,'Bài chỉ có tệp PDF: mở bản tin công ty ở khung bên trái, đọc và trả lời 4 câu hỏi.',NULL,'MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 09:00:00','2026-09-01 09:00:00'),(3010,9,19,3,'Part 7: Memo — New Supply Ordering Process',NULL,'Đọc bản ghi nhớ về quy trình đặt văn phòng phẩm và trả lời 3 câu hỏi.','**MEMO**\nTo: All department assistants\nFrom: Gregory Hale, Office Services\nDate: October 2\nRe: Ordering office supplies\n\nBeginning October 15, all requests for office supplies must be submitted through the new online ordering portal. Paper request forms will no longer be accepted after that date.\n\nThe portal lists every item in our approved catalog, including printer paper, toner cartridges, and filing folders. Each department has a monthly spending limit, which is displayed at the top of the order page. Orders that exceed this limit will be forwarded to the department head for approval.\n\nOrders placed before noon on Tuesday will be delivered on Thursday of the same week. Please combine requests from your team into a single weekly order whenever possible to reduce delivery costs.\n\nA short video tutorial is available on the company intranet. If you have trouble logging in, contact the help desk at extension 4410.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 10:00:00','2026-09-01 10:00:00'),(3011,11,23,3,'Part 7: Purchase Order and E-mail — Dental Supplies',NULL,'Đọc đơn đặt hàng và e-mail của nhà cung cấp (hai tab), rồi trả lời 5 câu hỏi.','## Purchase Order #PO-5517\nBayside Dental Clinic\nOrder date: November 3\nSupplier: Mercer Medical Supply\n\n| Item | Quantity | Unit price | Total |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Disposable gloves (box of 100) | 20 | $8.50 | $170.00 |\n| Face masks (box of 50) | 15 | $6.00 | $90.00 |\n| Dental bibs (pack of 500) | 4 | $22.00 | $88.00 |\n| Sterilization pouches (box of 200) | 6 | $14.00 | $84.00 |\n\nOrder total: $432.00\nRequested delivery: by November 10\nApproved by: Dr. Alan Pierce, Clinic Director\n\n## E-mail\nTo: Monica Reyes, Bayside Dental Clinic\nFrom: Jordan Wells, Mercer Medical Supply\nDate: November 5\nSubject: Order PO-5517\n\nDear Ms. Reyes,\n\nThank you for your recent order. All items have been packed except the sterilization pouches, which are temporarily out of stock. We expect a new shipment from the manufacturer on November 12 and will send the pouches separately at no extra shipping cost.\n\nThe rest of your order will arrive on November 8. Because your total exceeds $400, a 5 percent discount has been applied to your invoice.\n\nPlease let me know if you would like to change any part of this order.\n\nSincerely,\nJordan Wells\nCustomer Accounts','MARKDOWN','PART_7','DOUBLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 11:00:00','2026-09-01 11:00:00'),(3012,1000,1001,3,'Đọc hiểu: Notice — Lost and Found',NULL,'Đọc thông báo ngắn và trả lời 2 câu hỏi. Chú ý danh từ và đại từ chỉ đồ vật, người.','## Lost and Found at Maple Street Office\n\nEvery week, our reception desk collects a surprising number of items left behind in meeting rooms, the kitchen, and the lobby. Last month alone, staff found twelve umbrellas, five water bottles, three phone chargers, and one very expensive pair of headphones.\n\nAll items are kept in a locked cabinet behind the reception desk for thirty days. If you think something belongs to you, please describe it to the receptionist, who will check the cabinet for you. For valuable items such as wallets or laptops, you will be asked to show your employee ID.\n\nAfter thirty days, unclaimed items are donated to a local charity. Please help us by writing your name on your belongings, especially chargers and water bottles.','MARKDOWN','GENERAL','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 12:00:00','2026-09-01 12:00:00'),(3013,1002,1006,3,'Part 7: Text Messages — Planning a Team Lunch',NULL,'Đọc tin nhắn (chú ý cách dùng will / be going to) và trả lời 2 câu hỏi.','**Nadia Flores (9:02 A.M.)**\nHi Ben, are you going to book the restaurant for Friday\'s team lunch, or should I?\n\n**Ben Carter (9:05 A.M.)**\nI\'ll do it this morning. I\'m going to try Olivetto Bistro first because it\'s close to the office.\n\n**Nadia Flores (9:06 A.M.)**\nGood idea. Remember that Sam and Lucy don\'t eat meat.\n\n**Ben Carter (9:20 A.M.)**\nJust called them. They\'re fully booked at noon, but they have a table for ten at 12:30. They also have a vegetarian menu.\n\n**Nadia Flores (9:22 A.M.)**\n12:30 works. Our client call ends at noon anyway. I\'ll send the calendar invitation to the whole team after lunch today.\n\n**Ben Carter (9:23 A.M.)**\nGreat. I\'ll confirm the reservation now and ask them to prepare a few vegetarian dishes in advance.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 13:00:00','2026-09-01 13:00:00'),(3014,1004,1010,3,'Part 6: Notice — Library Self-Checkout Machines',NULL,'Chọn đáp án đúng cho các chỗ trống (131)–(134). Chú ý phân biệt tính từ và trạng từ.','**Attention, Library Visitors**\n\nStarting Monday, March 3, the Eastview Public Library will offer four new self-checkout machines near the main entrance. These machines allow visitors to borrow books (131) ------- without waiting in line at the front desk.\n\nTo use a machine, simply scan your library card and place your books on the reading pad. The screen will display your due dates, and a receipt will be printed (132) -------. You can also choose to have the receipt sent to your e-mail address instead.\n\nLibrary staff will be available all week to help visitors who are using the machines for the first time. (133) -------.\n\nWe believe this service will make your visits more (134) -------. The front desk will remain open for questions, membership renewals, and special requests. As always, thank you for supporting your local library.','MARKDOWN','PART_6','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 14:00:00','2026-09-01 14:00:00'),(3015,1004,1011,3,'Part 7: Notice and Flyer — Building Fitness Room',NULL,'Đọc thông báo và tờ rơi đính kèm (ảnh) rồi trả lời 3 câu hỏi.','## Notice to Employees of the Carlton Building\n\nWe are pleased to announce that the new fitness room on the basement level will open next month. The room was created from a former storage area and has been fully renovated with new flooring, lighting, and air conditioning.\n\nThe fitness room will be available free of charge to everyone who works in the Carlton Building. To enter, you will need to register your employee ID card at the security desk in the main lobby. Registration begins on Monday, and only registered cards will open the fitness room door.\n\nLockers are available, but users must bring their own locks. Towels will not be provided. Please see the attached flyer for opening hours and the class schedule.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 15:00:00','2026-09-01 15:00:00'),(3016,1005,1013,3,'Part 6: E-mail — Order Delay',NULL,'Chọn đáp án đúng cho các chỗ trống (131)–(134) trong e-mail gửi khách hàng.','To: Daniel Moore\nFrom: Brightline Home Goods\nDate: February 20\nSubject: Your order #84721\n\nDear Mr. Moore,\n\nThank you for shopping with Brightline Home Goods. We are writing to let you know that the desk lamp you ordered on February 16 has been (131) ------- delayed. Our supplier has informed us that the item will not arrive at our warehouse until February 27.\n\nWe understand that you may need the lamp soon. (132) -------. If you choose to wait, we will ship the lamp by express delivery at no (133) ------- cost. Alternatively, you may cancel the order and receive a full refund within three business days.\n\nTo cancel your order or choose a different item, simply reply to this e-mail. We apologize for the (134) ------- and appreciate your understanding.\n\nSincerely,\nBrightline Customer Care','MARKDOWN','PART_6','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 16:00:00','2026-09-01 16:00:00'),(3017,1005,1014,3,'Part 7: Article — Turning Travel Time into Study Time',NULL,'Đọc bài báo ngắn về cách tự học và trả lời 3 câu hỏi.','## Turning Travel Time into Study Time\n\nFor many office workers, the daily commute is the least productive part of the day. However, a recent survey by the Urban Learning Institute found that one in four commuters now uses travel time to study a language or develop a professional skill.\n\nMobile apps have made this much easier. Short lessons of five to ten minutes fit neatly between train stations, and many apps allow users to download content for areas with poor internet connection. Audio courses are especially popular among drivers, who cannot look at a screen.\n\nExperts recommend setting a clear and realistic goal. \"Studying for fifteen minutes every day is more effective than studying for two hours once a week,\" says Dr. Mei Tanaka, a learning researcher at the institute. She also suggests reviewing new vocabulary on the trip home, when the morning\'s material is still fresh.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 17:00:00','2026-09-01 17:00:00'),(3018,1006,1016,3,'Part 7: Job Posting — Customer Success Coordinator',NULL,'Đọc tin tuyển dụng (chú ý mệnh đề quan hệ which / who) và trả lời 3 câu hỏi.','## Customer Success Coordinator — Halvorsen Software\n\nHalvorsen Software, which develops scheduling tools for clinics and salons, is looking for a Customer Success Coordinator to join its growing team in Denver.\n\nThe coordinator will be the main contact for new customers during their first ninety days. Responsibilities include running online training sessions, answering questions by phone and e-mail, and collecting feedback that our product team uses to improve the software.\n\nCandidates who have at least two years of experience in customer service are preferred. Knowledge of Spanish is a plus, as many of our clients are based in Latin America. The position is full-time, and employees may work from home up to two days a week.\n\nTo apply, send a résumé and a short cover letter to careers@halvorsen.io by July 21. Interviews will be held during the first week of August.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 18:00:00','2026-09-01 18:00:00'),(3019,1008,1022,3,'Part 6: Memo — Updated Travel Policy',NULL,'Chọn đáp án đúng cho các chỗ trống (131)–(134) trong bản ghi nhớ.','**MEMO**\nTo: All staff\nFrom: Finance Department\nDate: January 8\nSubject: Changes to travel reimbursement\n\nEffective February 1, employees traveling on company business will be reimbursed through our new expense app, TripLedger. The app replaces the paper forms that many of you have used for years, and it will (131) ------- the time needed to process claims.\n\nTo receive payment, employees must upload a photo of each receipt (132) ------- seven days of returning from a trip. Claims submitted after this period may be delayed or rejected.\n\nPlease note that the daily meal allowance will increase from $45 to $55. (133) -------. Hotel costs, however, will continue to require approval from a manager before booking.\n\nA training session on TripLedger will be held on January 22. Employees who travel (134) ------- are strongly encouraged to attend.','MARKDOWN','PART_6','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 19:00:00','2026-09-01 19:00:00'),(3020,1008,1023,3,'Part 6: Business Letter — Supplier Partnership',NULL,'Chọn đáp án đúng cho các chỗ trống (131)–(134) trong thư thương mại.','Dear Ms. Alvarez,\n\nThank you for meeting with our team last week to discuss a possible partnership between Corbett Paper Company and your chain of office supply stores. We were (131) ------- impressed by your plans to open six new locations next year.\n\nAs promised, I have enclosed our latest product catalog and a price list for wholesale orders. Stores that order more than 500 cases per month (132) ------- for an additional 8 percent discount.\n\nWe would also be happy to supply your stores with display shelves at no cost. (133) -------. Our sales representatives can install them during regular business hours.\n\nI will contact you next Tuesday to answer any questions you may have. (134) -------, please feel free to call me directly at 555-0187.\n\nSincerely,\nHoward Bennett\nSales Director, Corbett Paper Company','MARKDOWN','PART_6','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 20:00:00','2026-09-01 20:00:00'),(3021,1010,1029,3,'Part 7: Announcement — Internal Job Openings',NULL,'Đọc thông báo nhân sự và trả lời 4 câu hỏi (có câu từ đồng nghĩa và câu chèn câu).','## Internal Job Openings: Apply Before Outside Candidates\n\nStarting this quarter, Linwood Pharmaceuticals will post all new positions on the company intranet for ten business days before advertising them to the public. [1] This change gives current employees the first opportunity to apply for roles that match their skills and career goals.\n\nEmployees who wish to apply must have worked at Linwood for at least twelve months and must inform their current supervisor before submitting an application. [2] Applications are reviewed by the hiring manager and a representative from Human Resources.\n\n\"We have many talented people who want to grow with the company,\" said Grace Holloway, vice president of Human Resources. [3] \"Promoting from within also helps new managers understand our culture from day one.\"\n\nEmployees who are not selected will receive individual feedback and may be offered a place in the company\'s leadership training program. [4] A full list of current openings can be found under \"Careers\" on the intranet home page.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 21:00:00','2026-09-01 21:00:00'),(3022,1011,1030,3,'Part 7: Advertisement and E-mail — Coworking Space',NULL,'Đọc quảng cáo và e-mail (hai tab), trả lời 5 câu hỏi; có câu phải đối chiếu hai văn bản.','## Advertisement\n**The Foundry Coworking — Now Open in Midtown**\n\nNeed a professional place to work without signing a long lease? The Foundry offers flexible memberships for freelancers and small teams.\n\n- Day Pass: $25 per day — access to shared desks from 8 A.M. to 6 P.M.\n- Flex Membership: $180 per month — 10 days of access per month, plus 2 hours of meeting room use\n- Resident Membership: $350 per month — your own reserved desk, 24-hour access, and 8 hours of meeting room use\n\nAll memberships include high-speed Wi-Fi, printing, and free coffee. Sign up before September 30 and receive your first week free.\n\n## E-mail\nTo: info@thefoundrymidtown.com\nFrom: Olivia Grant\nDate: September 26\nSubject: Membership question\n\nHello,\n\nI am a freelance translator, and I usually work from home, but I need a quiet place to meet clients about twice a month. I would need a desk about three days a week, and I often work late in the evening when deadlines are close.\n\nCould you tell me which membership would be best for me? I would also like to know whether I could bring a client to the meeting room without paying an extra fee.\n\nThank you,\nOlivia Grant','MARKDOWN','PART_7','DOUBLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 22:00:00','2026-09-01 22:00:00'),(3023,1011,1031,3,'Part 7: Three Texts — Riverside Hotel Reopening',NULL,'Đọc bài báo, e-mail và bảng giá (ba tab). Trả lời 5 câu hỏi, chú ý câu suy luận và đối chiếu.','## Article\n**Riverside Hotel to Reopen After Major Renovation**\n\nPORTVILLE — The Riverside Hotel, one of the city\'s oldest hotels, will reopen on April 1 after an eight-month renovation. The project added a rooftop restaurant, enlarged the conference center, and replaced the furniture in all 120 guest rooms.\n\nGeneral manager Felix Moreau said the hotel hopes to attract more business travelers. \"Our new conference center can now host events for up to 300 people,\" he said. Before the renovation, the largest room held only 150 guests.\n\n## E-mail\nTo: Felix Moreau\nFrom: Anita Shah, Brightway Events\nDate: February 10\nSubject: Conference booking\n\nDear Mr. Moreau,\n\nI am organizing the annual meeting of the Regional Accountants\' Association, which will take place on April 18 and 19. We expect about 250 attendees. Last year, we had to split our members between two hotels because we could not find a single venue large enough.\n\nCould you send me information about room rates for attendees and the cost of renting the conference center for two days?\n\nBest regards,\nAnita Shah\n\n## Price list\n**Riverside Hotel — Conference Center Rates (from April 1)**\n\n| Space | Capacity | Daily rate |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harbor Suite | Up to 80 guests | $1,200 |\n| Lighthouse Hall | Up to 150 guests | $2,600 |\n| Grand Ballroom | Up to 300 guests | $4,800 |\n\nGroups that book ten or more guest rooms receive 15 percent off the daily rate.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','TRIPLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-01 23:00:00','2026-09-01 23:00:00'),(3024,1013,1037,3,'Part 7: Article — The Two-List Method',NULL,'Đọc bài báo về quản lý thời gian và trả lời 4 câu hỏi (có câu chèn câu [1]–[4]).','## The Two-List Method for Busy Managers\n\nMany managers start each day with a long to-do list, only to find that half of it is still unfinished in the evening. Productivity coach Daniel Reyes believes the problem is not the length of the list but the lack of priorities.\n\nIn his new book, *Finish What Matters*, Mr. Reyes describes a simple approach he calls the \"two-list method.\" [1] Each morning, managers write down no more than three tasks that must be completed that day. All other tasks go on a second list, which is reviewed only after the first list is done.\n\nMr. Reyes tested the method with forty managers at a regional bank. [2] After eight weeks, participants reported finishing their most important tasks on time 30 percent more often than before. Several also said they felt less stressed at the end of the workday.\n\nThe method is not perfect. Some participants found it difficult to choose only three tasks when urgent requests arrived during the day. [3] Mr. Reyes recommends keeping one free hour in the afternoon to handle these unexpected items. [4]','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 00:00:00','2026-09-02 00:00:00'),(3025,1015,1044,3,'Đọc hiểu: Notice — Free Pronunciation Clinic',NULL,'Đọc thông báo về buổi luyện phát âm và trả lời 2 câu hỏi.','## Free Pronunciation Clinic for TOEIC Learners\n\nDo you sometimes confuse words like \"thirteen\" and \"thirty,\" or \"walk\" and \"work\"? Many learners can understand these words when they read them but find it difficult to hear the difference in a fast conversation.\n\nThis Saturday, the Language Center at Wexford College will hold a free pronunciation clinic for adult learners. Instructor Paula Grant, who has taught English in four countries, will explain how stress and vowel length change the meaning of similar-sounding words. Participants will then practice in small groups using short recordings from airport announcements, office meetings, and phone messages.\n\nThe clinic runs from 10:00 A.M. to 12:30 P.M. in Room 105. Seats are limited to twenty-five people, so please reserve a place by e-mailing clinic@wexford.edu before Thursday.','MARKDOWN','GENERAL','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 01:00:00','2026-09-02 01:00:00'),(3026,1017,1050,3,'Đọc hiểu: In-Store Announcement',NULL,'Đọc thông báo trong siêu thị (có thể luyện đọc to) và trả lời 2 câu hỏi.','## In-Store Announcement\n\nGood evening, shoppers, and thank you for choosing Fairway Market. We would like to remind you that the store will close in thirty minutes, at 9:00 P.M. Please bring your final selections to the checkout area at the front of the store.\n\nTonight only, all fresh bread and pastries in our bakery department are 50 percent off. Members of our Fairway Rewards program can also earn double points on every purchase made before closing time.\n\nIf you need help carrying heavy items to your car, please ask any staff member in a green apron. Starting next Monday, our new opening hours will be 7:00 A.M. to 10:00 P.M. every day. We look forward to seeing you again soon.','MARKDOWN','GENERAL','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 02:00:00','2026-09-02 02:00:00'),(3027,1020,1055,3,'Part 7: Article — Factory Rooftops Turn Solar',NULL,'Đọc bài báo (chú ý mệnh đề rút gọn: Faced with…, Having seen…) và trả lời 4 câu hỏi.','## Manufacturer Turns Rooftops into Power Plants\n\nHALDEN — Faced with rising electricity prices, Norvik Components has installed more than 4,000 solar panels on the roofs of its three factories in the Halden industrial park. Completed in June, the project now supplies about 35 percent of the company\'s electricity needs.\n\nThe panels, manufactured by a local supplier, were installed in stages so that production would not be interrupted. Workers fitted one building at a time, mostly during weekends and night shifts.\n\nAccording to chief operating officer Ingrid Solberg, the investment is expected to pay for itself within seven years. Having seen the results, two neighboring companies have already contacted Norvik to learn about the installation process.\n\nThe company plans to add battery storage next year, allowing the factories to use solar power collected during the day after sunset. Ms. Solberg noted that the batteries would also protect production lines during power outages, which have become more frequent in the region.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 03:00:00','2026-09-02 03:00:00'),(3028,1021,1056,3,'Part 7: Three Texts — Translation Services',NULL,'Đọc trang web, e-mail và đánh giá của khách (ba tab), trả lời 5 câu hỏi đối chiếu.','## Web page\n**Lumen Language Services — Pricing**\n\nLumen provides professional translation for businesses in more than 30 languages. All projects are completed by native speakers and checked by a second translator.\n\n| Service | Price | Delivery |\n|---|---|---|\n| Standard | $0.12 per word | 5 business days |\n| Priority | $0.18 per word | 2 business days |\n| Express | $0.25 per word | Within 24 hours |\n\nNew clients receive 10 percent off their first order. Documents longer than 20,000 words are quoted individually.\n\n## E-mail\nTo: orders@lumenlanguage.com\nFrom: Kenji Watanabe, Arcadia Outdoor Gear\nDate: March 3\nSubject: Catalog translation\n\nHello,\n\nOur company is launching its products in Germany next month, and we need our 9,000-word product catalog translated from English into German. The printer needs the final text by March 8, which is five business days from today, but we would like a few days to review the translation ourselves before then.\n\nThis will be our first time working with your company. Please confirm the total price.\n\nKenji Watanabe\n\n## Review\n**Client review — posted March 20**\n\nLumen did an excellent job on our catalog. The German text was accurate and natural, and the translator even pointed out two product names that could sound strange to German customers. The only problem was that the invoice was sent to our old address, but the accounting team fixed it quickly.\n— K. Watanabe, Arcadia Outdoor Gear','MARKDOWN','PART_7','TRIPLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 04:00:00','2026-09-02 04:00:00'),(3029,1021,1057,3,'Part 7: Lease Agreement and E-mail',NULL,'Đọc trích đoạn hợp đồng thuê và e-mail (hai tab), trả lời 5 câu hỏi về từ vựng hợp đồng.','## Lease excerpt\n**Commercial Lease Agreement — Section 7: Renewal and Termination**\n\n7.1 This lease shall remain in effect for a term of three years, beginning on May 1.\n\n7.2 The Tenant may renew the lease for an additional three-year term by giving written notice to the Landlord no later than ninety days before the end of the current term.\n\n7.3 Either party may terminate this agreement early by providing written notice at least six months in advance. If the Tenant terminates the lease early, the security deposit will not be returned.\n\n7.4 Rent for any renewal term shall not increase by more than 4 percent per year.\n\n## E-mail\nTo: Robert Fenwick, Fenwick Properties\nFrom: Alicia Duran, Duran Floral Design\nDate: January 20\nSubject: Lease at 48 Market Street\n\nDear Mr. Fenwick,\n\nOur three-year lease for the shop at 48 Market Street ends on April 30 of next year. We have been very happy with the location, and our business has grown steadily, so we would like to continue renting the space for another term.\n\nHowever, we may need a larger workshop within the next two years. If that happens, would you consider allowing us to move to the empty unit next door instead of ending the lease?\n\nKind regards,\nAlicia Duran','MARKDOWN','PART_7','DOUBLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 05:00:00','2026-09-02 05:00:00'),(3030,1022,1059,3,'Part 7: Memo and Newsletter (PDF) — Northbridge Logistics',NULL,'Đọc bản ghi nhớ và bản tin PDF đính kèm, trả lời 4 câu hỏi (có câu đối chiếu với PDF).','**MEMO**\nTo: Dispatch and warehouse supervisors\nFrom: Carla Duarte, Operations Manager\nDate: September 20\nSubject: Staffing in October\n\nAs announced in the latest issue of *The Northbridge Bulletin*, all warehouse staff must attend the annual safety training at the head office. Please arrange your team schedules so that no more than half of each shift attends the morning session. The remaining staff will attend the repeat session in the afternoon.\n\nBecause the new Millford warehouse is now fully operational, we will temporarily move six drivers from the Eastgate depot to Millford during October. Supervisors at Eastgate should send me the names of volunteers by September 27.\n\nFinally, I would like to thank everyone in Dispatch for adopting Samuel\'s route-planning spreadsheet so quickly. It has already made a noticeable difference in our delivery times.','MARKDOWN','PART_7','SINGLE','PUBLISHED','2026-09-02 06:00:00','2026-09-02 06:00:00');
